course: dictionary
lesson: 14999
title: What a requirement means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A requirement is something you must have or must do. It is a rule that has to be met before you can go on. «To join the club, you must meet the requirements: be ten years old and bring a signed form.» The club will not let you in until you meet them.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Words like must, need and have to tell you a requirement is coming. Ask yourself: what does this demand? If you cannot get in, pass or finish without it, it is a requirement. Then swap in «a rule that must be met» and check the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Requirements show up at school and in everyday life. «The entry requirements for the school include a reading test.» A helmet can be a requirement for riding a bike on some roads. «Wear a helmet: it is a requirement on this road.»
fact: A requirement is something you must have or must do.
fact: «Requirement» is a noun. The plural is requirements.
fact: Useful phrases: «meet the requirements», «a minimum requirement», «entry requirements».
fact: A minimum requirement is the least you need: «a minimum requirement of 50 marks» means you need at least 50.
fact: In maths and exams, a question's requirements are what it asks you to give, such as «show your working».
exercise: «The club has one requirement: you must be ten years old.» What is a requirement here? | A kind of club uniform | A prize you win | *Something you must have or do | A type of game
exercise: «The entry requirements for the school include a reading test.» What do the entry requirements say? | What the school serves for lunch | *What must be done to get in | How many children are in each class | When the holidays start
exercise: «A helmet is a requirement for cycling on some roads.» What does a helmet mean here? | It is a game you play | It is a nice colour to wear | *It is something you must have to ride there | It is a bell for your bike
test: «To pass the course, you must meet the requirements.» What does meet the requirements mean? | Lose your books | Leave early | *Do what must be done to pass | Win a race against the others
test: Which word means the least you need to reach? | Surplus | *Minimum | Maximum | Bonus
exam: Mia says a requirement is a reward for trying hard. Is she right? | Yes, it is a prize | *No, a requirement is something you must have or do | Yes, it means the same as a holiday | No, it is a colour
